{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"OESA-2026-4767","published":"2026-11-11T12:25:57Z","modified":"2026-11-11T12:45:11.079987647Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-105924","CVE-2026-105946","CVE-2026-107157"],"summary":"qt6-qtbase security update","details":"Qt is a software toolkit for developing applications.\r\n\r\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\nA NULL pointer dereference vulnerability in the Qt QCborValue to JSON conversion of the Qt Core module.(CVE-2026-105924)\n\nOut-of-bounds read in the QAuthenticator NTLM authentication handling in the Qt Network module in Qt Group Qt allows remote attackers to obtain sensitive information (heap memory contents) or cause a denial of service (application crash) via a crafted NTLM challenge sent by a malicious server or proxy, when an application using QNetworkAccessManager or QTcpSocket authenticates with NTLM.(CVE-2026-105946)\n\nSpecially crafted CBOR input passed to QCborValue::fromCbor() in Qt Core can cause an out-of-bounds read, which may crash the application and could expose information.(CVE-2026-107157)","affected":[{"package":{"name":"qt6-qtbase","ecosystem":"openEuler:24.03-LTS-SP4","purl":"pkg:rpm/openEuler/qt6-qtbase&distro=openEuler-24.03-LTS-SP4"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"6.5.2-18.oe2403sp4"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"aarch64":["qt6-qtbase-6.5.2-18.oe2403sp4.aarch64.rpm","qt6-qtbase-debuginfo-6.5.2-18.oe2403sp4.aarch64.rpm","qt6-qtbase-debugsource-6.5.2-18.oe2403sp4.aarch64.rpm","qt6-qtbase-devel-6.5.2-18.oe2403sp4.aarch64.rpm","qt6-qtbase-examples-6.5.2-18.oe2403sp4.aarch64.rpm","qt6-qtbase-gui-6.5.2-18.oe2403sp4.aarch64.rpm","qt6-qtbase-ibase-6.5.2-18.oe2403sp4.aarch64.rpm","qt6-qtbase-mysql-6.5.2-18.oe2403sp4.aarch64.rpm","qt6-qtbase-odbc-6.5.2-18.oe2403sp4.aarch64.rpm","qt6-qtbase-postgresql-6.5.2-18.oe2403sp4.aarch64.rpm","qt6-qtbase-private-devel-6.5.2-18.oe2403sp4.aarch64.rpm","qt6-qtbase-static-6.5.2-18.oe2403sp4.aarch64.rpm"],"noarch":["qt6-qtbase-common-6.5.2-18.oe2403sp4.noarch.r